  "passenger_render": "Real player/entity, seated under the drone; preserve player skin, armour and identity. Apply a seated rescue pose with bent knees, hips at the specified anchor. Do not spawn the fitting mannequin.",
  "physics": "Use existing Drone Warfare aerial drone controller/physics and existing SBW-compatible infrastructure. Do not apply the tracked rover physics or a fixed flight-attitude override.",
  "runtime_requirements": [
    "Separate controller at monitor and carried passenger: operator remains at the monitor.",
    "Server-authoritative attachment: one real passenger, synchronized vehicle ID and attachment state; reject duplicate mounting.",
    "Only attach through explicit interaction; do not automatically grab by proximity.",
    "Suspend actual passenger from harness_sway: same interpolated transform for all harness geometry and player.",
    "F5 cycle: front monitor camera, rear third person, overhead; camera positions and bounds based on the aircraft, not the operator.",
    "Lower/retract runtime cable procedurally from fairlead to suspension eye; keep the line connected. Provided asset uses one fixed lowered presentation length. Do not animate only the passenger and leave the strap behind.",
    "Release near a valid ground location; restore normal player pose/camera on dismount, death, disconnect, destruction and world reload.",
    "Before touchdown, lower/release the passenger or provide a properly fitted runtime hoist/retracted pose. Default hanging passenger extends below landing skids.",
    "Use body and rotor extents for clearance checks. Cosmetic render meshes are not collision shapes.",
    "All five clips are cosmetic previews; winch drum clip does not retract the line or implement a hoist.",
    "Use native mesh-capable renderer; cube-only Bedrock/Java export loses geometry. Animation JSON alone is not a complete Minecraft model."
  ],
